## 3. Set Up Google Authentication

To allow your users to log in with a single click using their Google accounts, you need to link Google Cloud with Supabase.

### Step A: Get Google Credentials
1. Go to the [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/).
2. Create a new project (or use an existing one).
3. Go to **APIs & Services -> Credentials**.
4. Click **Create Credentials -> OAuth client ID**.
5. If prompted, configure the **OAuth consent screen** first (set it to External, fill in the app name, and save).
6. For **Application type**, select **Web application**.
7. Name it something like "Smart Chess Login".
8. Under **Authorized redirect URIs**, you need to add your Supabase redirect URL. 
   - You can find this in your Supabase Dashboard under **Authentication -> URL Configuration** -> **Site URL** (e.g., `https://<your-project-id>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback`).
9. Click **Create**. Google will give you a **Client ID** and a **Client Secret**. Keep these handy.

### Step B: Enable Google in Supabase
1. Go back to your [Supabase Dashboard](https://supabase.com/dashboard).
2. Navigate to **Authentication -> Providers**.
3. Select **Google** from the list.
4. Toggle **Enable Sign in with Google** to ON.
5. Paste the **Client ID** and **Client Secret** you just got from Google Cloud.
6. Click **Save**.

---

## 4. Set Up Razorpay Payments

To accept payments, you need to link your backend to your Razorpay account.

1. Log into your [Razorpay Dashboard](https://dashboard.razorpay.com/).
2. In the left sidebar, navigate to **Account & Settings** -> **API Keys** (under the "Website and App Settings" section).
3. Click **Generate Key** (or "Generate Test Key" if you are still testing).
4. Razorpay will show you a pop-up containing your **Key Id** and **Key Secret**. Do not close this pop-up yet!
5. In the `Backend` folder of this codebase, create a new file named `.env` and add your keys:
```env
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=your_key_id_here
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=your_key_secret_here
```
6. In the `Frontend` folder, open your `.env` file and add the Key ID there too (so the checkout popup knows which account to use):
```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=your_key_id_here
```
7. Save both files.

---

**That's it!** You can now run the application locally (start the backend with Python and the frontend with `npm run dev`) and your Google login and payment infrastructure will be fully operational.
